/* book Worked example: Q: A steam plant takes steam at 60 bar and 500 °C. In a reheat cycle the steam expands to 10 bar, is reheated to 500 °C and expands to the condenser at 0.1 bar. Find the exhaust dryness, the net work, the heat added and the efficiency, and compare them with the simple cycle between 60 bar, 500 °C and 0.1 bar.
   1. State 1 (60 bar, 500 °C): h₁ = 3423.1 kJ/kg, s₁ = 6.8826 kJ/kg·K.
   2. State 2: s₂ = 6.8826 is above sg = 6.585 at 10 bar, so the HP exhaust is superheated; interpolating in the 10 bar table gives h₂ = 2920.4 kJ/kg (about 240 °C).
   3. State 3 (10 bar, 500 °C): h₃ = 3479.1 kJ/kg, s₃ = 7.7641 kJ/kg·K.
   4. State 4 at 0.1 bar: x₄ = (7.7641 − 0.6492)/7.4996 = 0.9487; h₄ = 191.81 + 0.9487 × 2392.1 = 2461.2 kJ/kg.
   5. Pump: wP = 0.001010 × (6000 − 10) = 6.05 kJ/kg; h₆ = 191.81 + 6.05 = 197.86 kJ/kg.
   6. wT = (3423.1 − 2920.4) + (3479.1 − 2461.2) = 502.7 + 1017.9 = 1520.6 kJ/kg; wnet = 1514.6 kJ/kg.
   7. qin = (3423.1 − 197.86) + (3479.1 − 2920.4) = 3225.2 + 558.7 = 3783.9 kJ/kg; η = 1514.6/3783.9 = 0.400.
   8. Simple cycle: x = (6.8826 − 0.6492)/7.4996 = 0.831, h = 2180.0 kJ/kg, wnet = 1243.1 − 6.05 = 1237.1 kJ/kg, qin = 3225.2 kJ/kg, η = 0.384.
   Answer: With reheat: exhaust dryness 0.949, wnet = 1514.6 kJ/kg, qin = 3783.9 kJ/kg, η = 40.0%, steam rate 2.38 kg/kWh. Without: dryness 0.831, 1237.1 kJ/kg, η = 38.4%, 2.91 kg/kWh. Reheat mainly dries the exhaust and raises the work per kg. */
