/* book exam traps: In the reheat cycle the heat added includes the reheater, (h₃ − h₂). Leaving it out gives η = 1514.6/3225.2 = 47.0%, an impossible jump. | In the regenerative cycle only (1 − m) kg goes through the condenser and pump 1. Multiplying every term by 1 kg overstates the turbine work and the heat rejected. | An open heater needs a pump after it, because the heater is at the bleed pressure, not the boiler pressure. A sketch with one pump before the heater and none after it is wrong. | Check whether the steam at a bleed or reheat pressure is wet or superheated before choosing the table: compare s with sg at that pressure. | Reheat is for dryness and work; regeneration is for efficiency. Writing "reheat greatly raises efficiency" loses marks. */
